  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 229 AM MDT Fri Jul 24 2026\n\nEarly morning radar shows several showers and thunderstorms working \nnortheastward through the CWA. Within a couple of hours, we should \nsee a break in activity ahead of the afternoon push. The latest CAMs \nfeature increased storm coverage this afternoon than previous runs. \nTemperatures today will be noticeably warmer as they increase to \nwell-above normal again in the mid- to upper-90s across the low \nelevations and 80s in the mid-elevations and mountain valleys. A \nHEAT ADVISORY remains in effect today for many of our valley \nlocations, including the Snake River Plain, eastern Magic Valley, \nArco Desert, Shoshone region, and South Hills. Daytime temperature \nwill remain fairly stable through the entirety of the forecast \nperiod. A shortwave on Saturday will bring increased chances for \nshowers and thunderstorms in an otherwise dry-leaning pattern. Winds \nwill also increase on Saturday with many areas expected to observe \n30 to 40 mph gusts. Thus, elevated fire weather conditions are \nanticipated over the next couple of days whether it be for scattered \nthunderstorms or the combination of low min RH and winds as we \ncontinue to dry out.",
